.TITLE "rmdir"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Removes a directory. It deletes a folder from the filesystem, provided that the directory is empty unless specific flags are used.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**rd**

.DIV "TLDR"
**rmdir name**
Removes an empty directory with the specified name.
> __name__ the target directory name

**rmdir /s name**
Removes a directory and all its subdirectories and files.
> __/s__ recursive flag | __name__ the target directory name

**rmdir /s /q name**
Removes a directory tree silently without asking for confirmation.
> __/s__ recursive flag | __/q__ quiet flag | __name__ the target directory name

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Use the __/s__ flag with caution, as it permanently deletes all contents within a folder. Adding the __/q__ flag is useful for batch scripts where user interaction is not desired.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:mkdir** **windows:del**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/rmdir__
